.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt RSWC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rswc
.Nd retrieve files from the network
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Av46
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl T Ar timeout
.Ar url
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
retrieves files from the network.
the options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl A
do not follow redirects.
.It Fl v
enable verbose output.
.It Fl 4
use IPv4 addresses only.
.It Fl 6
use IPv6 addresses only.
.It Fl o Ar output
write the retrieved data to
.Ar output .
if
.Ar output
is
.Qq - ,
write to stdout.
.It Fl T Ar timeout
set the network timeout to
.Ar timeout
seconds.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
download a url:
.Dl $ rswc https://example.com/file.tar.gz
.Pp
download a url to a specific output:
.Dl $ rswc -o file.tgz https://example.com/file.tar.gz
.Pp
download a url with a fixed timeout:
.Dl $ rswc -T 30 https://example.com/file.tar.gz
.Pp
download a file using IPv6:
.Dl $ rswc -6 https://example.com/file.tar.gz
.Pp
download a file using IPv4:
.Dl $ rswc -4 https://example.com/file.tar.gz
.Pp
download a file with verbose output:
.Dl $ rswc -v https://example.com/file.tar.gz
